# Project Rules — Sovereign AI Trading Engine (NSE)

## Context
Quant trading system for Indian equities (NSE). Core pipeline: DataStore (yfinance → Parquet)
→ RegimeDetector (breadth/regime) → BrainA V5 (kill score) → ExecutionModel (dynamic sizing)
→ PortfolioConstraints → PortfolioEngine → structural exits (src/backtest/position.py).

Signal/sizing/risk logic (src/, tests/) is fully deterministic and must run without any API key
or network access. Only the Streamlit dashboard's BrainB commentary layer needs GEMINI_API_KEY,
and only the live scan/regime check in src/app_v6.py needs a Yahoo Finance connection.

## Non-negotiable constraints
- **Zero point-in-time leakage**: any indicator, regime call, or exit signal must only reference
  data available as-of the current bar. No forward-looking lookups into future rows of a DataFrame.
- **UTF-8 everywhere**: all file I/O must be explicit `encoding="utf-8"`. Never rely on platform default.
- **Risk multiplier limits are hard bounds, not defaults to tune away**: CONVICTION_MIN_MULT (0.75) /
  CONVICTION_MAX_MULT (1.25), MAX_DD_THRESHOLD (0.15), BREADTH_THRESHOLD (0.35) in src/config.py are
  institutional risk rails. Do not widen them without an explicit instruction from me — flag it instead.
- Never touch `src/config.py`'s `validate_config()` invariants without keeping them in sync with any
  new parameter you add — every new risk-relevant constant needs an assert.
- `src/data/store.py` and anything under `src/live_*` touches real market data / real money paths —
  treat changes there as higher-risk than research/backtest code.

## Coding standards
- Match existing style: plain functions/classes, no framework magic, pandas-vectorized where the
  codebase already does that (see src/regime.py, src/backtest/position.py).
- Keep new modules under the existing layout: src/backtest/, src/execution/, src/data/, src/utils/.
- Every new risk/sizing rule needs a corresponding test in tests/, following the pattern in
  tests/test_v7_logic.py (class-per-feature, method-per-case).

## Test commands
- Full suite (offline, no network/API key): `python -m pytest tests/ -v`
- Local full health check: `python scripts/verify_project.py`
- Config invariants only: `python -c "from src.config import validate_config; validate_config()"`

## When making changes
1. Run the full test suite before proposing anything as done.
2. If a change touches config.py, RS/breadth/DD thresholds, or position sizing math, say so explicitly
   and show the before/after values — don't bury a risk parameter change inside an unrelated diff.
3. Never invent a "dry run" of run_phase3_simulation.py / run_v7_simulation.py as passing unless you
   actually ran it — those scripts hit live Yahoo Finance and can fail for reasons unrelated to your change.
